<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates rise in all maturities.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates rise in all maturities.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) spiked up in all maturities on Wednesday, mirroring the tight domestic liquidity, traders said.</p>
<p>A foreign bank trader said banks were trying to generate liquidity through PHIBOR by selling their dollars in exchange for pesos.</p>
<p>Lenders of pesos have been raising their quotes, leading to the higher PHIBOR rates, he said.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			 SEPT 18		 SEPT 17</p>
<p>    1 W		12  1/2		 11 15/16</p>
<p>    2 W		12  3/8		 11 15/16</p>
<p>    1 M		12  5/16		11 13/16</p>
<p>    2 M		11 15/16		11  5/8</p>
<p>    3 M		11 13/16		11  9/16</p>
<p>    6 M		11 13/16		11  9/16</p>
<p>    12M		12			11 13/16</p>
<p>    VAL		19-Sep		  18-Sep</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom (632) 841-8937</p>
